Subject: [PATCH] Build only selected hardware drivers

Proposal 1 from https://github.com/domoticz/domoticz/issues/6748 (closed
upstream, kept here as a local patch).

cmake/HardwareModules.cmake maps every hardware type to its driver sources.
INCLUDE_HARDWARE_ALL=ON (default) builds everything as before. With
INCLUDE_HARDWARE_ALL=OFF only the modules switched on with
INCLUDE_HARDWARE_<NAME>=ON are compiled and linked; each enabled module
defines WITH_HW_<NAME>, which guards the places in the core that create or
call into a driver (AddHardwareFromParams, setpoint/thermostat dispatch,
forecast URLs, web handler registration, Kodi/LMS events).

Hardware of a type that is not built stays in the database, is not started
(AddHardwareFromParams logs an error) and is hidden from gethardwaretypes.

Always built: Domoticz remote server, dummy (createdevice), MQTT client
(MQTT push derives from it), RFXCOM/P1/Teleinfo/MySensors/Evohome base
classes, Python plugins (USE_PYTHON), OpenZWave (USE_OPENZWAVE).

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 17e95775..dafbbbc4 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -442,6 +442,9 @@ tinyxpath/xpath_static.cpp
 tinyxpath/xpath_syntax.cpp
 )
 
